title: Settings › Pause › Pause one agent, resume all
route: /settings
intro: Each row has its own switch. Turning one off pauses that agent: its row gets a 'Paused' tag and an amber banner names it and says what it holds back. The banner carries a 'Resume all agents' button.
dir: TD
also: The header button follows the count. It reads 'Resume all agents' only when all sixteen are paused. The switch's accessible name is the agent's name and whether it is paused or working.
---
screen s1 "Settings\nAll sixteen switches on. Header button reads 'Pause all agents'"
click c1 "Click a row's switch\nNo confirmation"
decision q1 "Was the switch on?"
store a1 "That agent is paused\nSwitch goes grey, 'Paused' tag beside its name"
toast a4 "'{Agent} paused'\nAmber toast"
store a2 "That agent is working again\nSwitch goes green, the tag goes"
toast a5 "'{Agent} resumed'\nGreen toast"
decision q2 "Are all sixteen now paused?"
process b1 "Header button stays 'Pause all agents'\nAmber banner '{Agent} is paused' or 'N agents are paused'\n'Paused: Verify and Reader.' then what each one holds back"
process b2 "Header button becomes 'Resume all agents'\nBanner reads 'All agents are paused'"
decision q3 "Is any agent still paused?"
process b3 "No banner\nHeader button reads 'Pause all agents'"
process b4 "Banner shrinks to the agents still paused"
click c2 "Click 'Pause all agents' while some are paused"
goto g1 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause all agents"
click c3 "Click 'Resume all agents'\nIn the banner, or in the header when all sixteen are paused"
store d1 "All sixteen agents are active again"
toast d2 "'Agents resumed'\nGreen toast"
end e1 "Page is back to normal"
goto g2 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › What the rest of the app shows"

s1 --> c1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| a1 --> a4 --> q2
q1 -->|No| a2 --> a5 --> q3
q2 -->|No| b1
q2 -->|Yes| b2
q3 -->|No| b3
q3 -->|Yes| b4
b1 --> c2 --> g1
b1 --> c3
b4 --> c3
b2 --> c3
c3 --> d1 & d2
d1 --> e1
d2 --> e1
b1 -.-> g2
b3 --> e1
